   "text": {
    "L1": "A mirror image flips a shape across a line. Every point stays the same distance from that line.",
    "L2": "Folding paper makes the fold a mirror line. When you open it, the cut shape appears on both sides.",
    "L3": "A copied shape is not enough. The shape must flip, so its details face the opposite way.",
    "L4": "For quarter-turn symmetry, repeat one motif around the same centre. Make four equally spaced copies.",
    "L5": "A design can have turn symmetry without a mirror line. A pinwheel is one example.",
    "L6": "Check mirror symmetry by folding. Check turn symmetry by turning a tracing around the centre.",
    "L7": "Now choose the design that has turn symmetry but no mirror line."
   },
